# Auto-push to GitHub

After making code changes in this project, commit and push to GitHub without waiting for the user to ask.

## Workflow

1. Finish the requested code changes.
2. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and `git log -1 --oneline` to review what will be committed.
3. Stage only relevant files (never `.env`, secrets, or `node_modules`).
4. Commit with a concise message focused on why.
5. Push to `origin main` (use `git pull --rebase origin main` first if the push is rejected).

## Remote

- Repository: `https://github.com/avolcanv1/volc4n.git`
- Branch: `main`

## Skip auto-push only when

- The user explicitly says not to push or commit.
- There are no file changes to commit.
- The change is exploratory and the user asked a question-only task with no edits.
